      "name": "Edit Fields (Data Cleaning)",
      "notes": "Normalizes and sanitizes incoming product data.\nTrims strings, converts numeric fields (current_stock, avg_daily_sales, reorder_threshold, unit_price) to proper types, and sets defaults for missing values.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 280,
        "content": "## WF-01: Product & Sales Data Ingestion\n\n**Trigger:** POST webhook `/product-sales-ingest`\n**Called by:** React frontend (AddProductModal, CsvImportModal)\n\n**Purpose:** Receives product/sales data from the store owner, cleans and normalizes the input, then upserts the product into the Supabase `Products` table.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Receive POST payload from frontend\n2. Clean & normalize fields (trim strings, parse numbers)\n3. Check if product_id already exists\n4. If exists → Update row | If new → Create row\n5. Return success response with action taken"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1400,
        -480
      ],
      "id": "sticky-wf01-overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 400,
        "height": 160,
        "content": "## Upsert Logic\n\nThe If node checks whether the Supabase query returned an existing product.\n- **True branch:** Product exists → Update row\n- **False branch:** New product → Create row\n\nBoth branches return a JSON response confirming the action taken."
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -700,
        -380
      ],
      "id": "sticky-wf01-upsert",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    }
  ],
